{"kind":"assert","text":"H3 family (b0bb536e): approved as proposed.\n1. Pins: `platform:register@30`, `platform:directory@29` and `platform:order@1` are free on published main. One test, apps/room/celld/mac/test/prepare-project.test.mjs line 45, uses `platform:register@30` as its unknown definition; move that test to a number no family will take (for example @999) in the same head.\n2. H3 owns canonical admission and fold of the three order tags: allocation, resolution and hole. Same pattern as the H2 ruling 1e80741a: the shared parser and keeper, existing record bounds, no Scope pin guard or H4 runtime change. `abandon` and the remaining unserved tags stay refused until their owner (H4) names them.\n3. Keep U1's Register 29, Directory 28 and Rules 16 untouched, keep the default host selection, and add no room to the new family in this head: no deploy changes a register root (memory of 18 Nov: a register switch strands rooms).\n4. The lineage extension admits only a digest-pinned installed lane in the new family creating its exact Order 1 child. Witness the refusal of the same create from a CF-1 lane, beside the passing pair.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}